there are many ways in which we can find  the HC F of two numbers but in this  video we will look at the prime factor  method let's say we want to find the HC  f of 24 and 36 what we need to do is  very simple  we just have to reduce the numbers to  its prime factors and we can do that  using upside-down division first let's  find the prime factors of 24 we draw two  lines like this now we think of all the  prime factors that 24 is divisible by we  start with 2 24 is divisible by 2 so we  write a 2 here 2 times 12 is 24  what about 12 is it divisible by 2 yes  12 is also divisible by 2 we write 2  again and draw a line 2 times 6 is 12 6  is also divisible by 2 and 2 times 3 is  6 we stop here as we got a prime factor  how can we write 24 now remember the  l-shape 24 can be written as 2 x 2 x 2 x  3 we reduce 24 to its prime factors we  do the same for 36 actually why don't  you try reducing 36 to its prime factors  pause the video and give it a shot 36 is  divisible by 2 and 2 times 18 is 36 18  is also divisible by 2 and 2 times 9 is  18 is 9 divisible by 2  no 9 is not divisible by 2 and we jump  to the next prime number which is 3 is 9  divisible by 3 yes 9 is divisible by 3 3  times 3 is 9 we stop here since it's a  prime factor 36 can be written as the  product of these 4 numbers 36 is equal  to 2 multiplied by 2  x 3 x 3 the difficult part is over but  how does this give us the HCF to find  the 8 CF all we have to do is multiply  the prime factors that are common to  both the numbers 2 is a common prime  factor to both the numbers so we write a  2 once there is another 2 that is common  to both so we multiply this 2 with  another 2 and there is a 3 which is  common to both the numbers as well hence  we multiply this product with 3 yes we  just multiplied the prime factors which  are common to both the numbers this  gives us the HCF 2 times 2 is 4 and 4  times 3 is 12 the highest common factor  of 24 and 36 is 12 this is the prime  factor method to find the highest common  factor of two numbers in the next  session we will solve for the 8 CF of 42  and 56  [Music]  you
 

